bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (base seed aa542919a298e130 = origin f43f68c218e, release/1.0.0, aarch64, JIT): enum Opt: Some(i64) | None; fn g(x) -> i64: match x: Some(v): v / None: -5; g(Opt.None) aborts on the JIT (match exhausted: the bare None arm over an untyped subject lowers to rt_is_none, which only knows nil and the builtin Option None), interpreter -5 (a bare None pattern matches any enum value whose variant is named None, interpreter_patterns.rs pattern_enum_name_matches). Same for a None-only enum (enum Q: Here(i64) | None), the expression match, and a case nil: arm (interpreter Expr::Nil also matches a None variant; JIT base 1 vs -5). Left open by seed_jit_any_match_bare_some_arm_takes_user_enum_unit_variant_2026-11-27."

