bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27, 2, "2026-11-27 follow-up: with 30 None-declaring enums a per-enum rt_enum_check_variant chain cost 1.96s vs base 0.17s (4e7 erased nil matches, Col.Red + raw subjects). The chain now reads rt_enum_discriminant once, compares it inline against the owners' None discriminants, and calls rt_enum_check_variant only within a matching discriminant group: seed 193d6b67d690b318, 3 alternated rounds vs base aa542919a298e130: 30 enums 0.43/0.35/0.38s vs 0.18/0.17/0.17s; no shaped enum 0.32/0.18/0.16 vs 0.26/0.17/0.14s; one None-only enum, raw subjects 0.21/0.24/0.20 vs 0.28/0.22/0.30s; Q.None subjects 0.54/0.65/0.50s (base aborts); RSS flat. Rust: seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs 15/15; 17 related compiler/tests binaries fail identically on base (erased_ints_reach_typed_i64_params_untagged, u64_optional_bindings_and_mutating_accessors_preserve_payloads, untyped_hir_expression_constructors_do_not_invent_type_metadata); lib 5182 pass, failures = base set plus the flaky repeated_import_of_the_same_module_parses_it_exactly_once (passes alone 3/3)."
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27, 3, "2026-11-27 review follow-up (final design): the line-2 chain let a bare None/nil arm match builtin Result values (rt_enum_check_variant treats an actual id 0 as a wildcard) and still cost 3.8s vs base 0.18s with 30 None-FIRST enums (Col.Red subject). Now one runtime membership predicate, rt_enum_none_set_query(value, set) (Rust value/objects.rs + C runtime_native.c twins; core_values.spl answers -1), answers nil / builtin None / owner None in one registry-validated read plus one probe of a lockless CAS table (16384 slots, probe bounded to 16; members store disc+1, a sealed miss caches -1). The set key is file + owner list, so every site of a module shares one set; capacity ~ modules x (owners + 1) + distinct non-owner ids seen. Unsealed (first query, full table, or core lane) calls one per-module __erased_none_arm_slow_<key> helper: rt_is_none, rt_enum_none_set_add per owner (id operand re-pointed by native qualification like rt_enum_check_variant's, mangle.rs call_carries_enum_id_operand), rt_enum_none_set_seal, then the exact rt_enum_check_variant chain behind the id < 2 split (Result -> no). The match function keeps 2 calls (outlining: seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27). Red -> green JIT: Result beside a Some|None enum 77777722 / -55555489 -> -54222278 (= interpreter); shared-discriminant owners 0 -> 110011001100; two-module 22122443442 -> 11122333442. Perf 4e8 matches, seed aa542919a298e130 vs 15eee0f57b83a3ac, 3 alternated rounds: 30 None-first enums 1.04 -> 1.47s (same-binary no-owner row 1.16s: +13% is binary layout, rt_is_none disassembles identically), builtin Some/None subject 1.12 -> 1.25s, no-owner 1.03 -> 1.15s, user None subject base wrong (80000000) -> 60000000 = interpreter."
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27, 4, "2026-11-27 fable-review redesign (supersedes the line-3 owner table, which is removed): the table cost +35% on a base-correct path (30 None-first enums, Col.Red subject, 4e8 matches: base 1460 ms, table 1969 ms) because any lookup keyed on the enum id adds work per user-enum subject. Now a user variant NAMED None is stamped at construction: codegen picks rt_enum_new_none instead of rt_enum_new when the MIR variant name is None and the enum id is >= 2 (codegen/shared.rs enum_constructor_symbol; cranelift EnumUnit/EnumWith + constructor-call fallback, LLVM EnumUnit/EnumWith, interpreter bridge runtime_bridge.rs, isolated-thread clone keeps the flag), which sets HeapHeader.reserved bit 0 (Rust) / RtCoreEnum.reserved2 bit 0 (C runtime_native.c; runtime.c weak twin and core_enum.spl build a plain value). The arm is one call, rt_is_none_variant(v) = rt_is_none(v) or the stamp (Rust + C twins; core_values.spl answers rt_is_none); rt_is_none ignores the stamp so a typed Q? holding Q.None stays present. No site key, table, seal, helper or id remap (mangle.rs back to base); matches by name like the interpreter, Result never stamped. A module with no None-declaring user enum keeps plain rt_is_none. Not covered: bytecode VM constructors and the core lane do not stamp (base behaviour there). Tests: seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs 19/19 (new: list/return/payload round trips, typed Q? guard), runtime none_variant_stamp_is_read_only_by_rt_is_none_variant, compiler lib erased_ 33/33, runtime lib 1578/1578; compiler lib 5177 pass / 24 fail, the 3 core-lane failures reproduce with the pre-change runtime sources. Probes p1-p4 JIT == interpreter on seed b45d80cfb2580c23 (base JIT: list/return/dict/payload 0, fix 1). Perf, 4e8 matches, min of 5 alternated rounds, ms, base aa542919a298e130 / table 15eee0f57b83a3ac / stamp b45d80cfb2580c23: 30 None-first enums Col.Red subject 1464 / 1979 / 1463; no None-owning enum 1459 / 1564 / 1462; same-code control (typed Col? subject, 30 enums) 1457 / 1564 / 1467 -- the table binary's +7% no-owner row is binary-wide (rt_is_none machine code byte-identical), not the lowering; raw subject 1209 / 1174 / 1119; E7.None subject 1485 (wrong answer) / 1967 / 1462. Construction (2e7 Q.None, 6 alternated rounds, s): base 4.80-5.20, stamp 5.14-5.67; same-code control Q.Other (rt_enum_new 0x7c bytes in both) base 4.87-5.46, stamp 5.15-5.58, so the spread is the binary, not the one extra store; RSS 0.96-0.99 GB both (pre-existing transient growth)."
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27, 5, "2026-11-27 fable-review follow-up to line 4: the stamp bit moved to HeapHeader.reserved bit 15 (RT_ENUM_FLAG_NONE_VARIANT = 1 << 15), disjoint from RT_STRING_FLAG_SHARED / _ASCII (bits 0-1) whose writers take any heap header (today they are only called on strings); rt_is_none_variant left runtime_symbol_is_codegen_root (it is always a MIR call), rt_enum_new_none stays there because codegen emits it; user_option_shaped_enums records only whether an enum declares None. New test runtime_bridge value_to_runtime_stamps_a_user_none_variant (interpreter -> runtime bridge stamps Q.None, not the builtin None nor Result). Seed 71311c5d76676ba8: probes p1/p2 identical on interpret, strict JIT and default mixed mode; p3/p4 differ only by the filed typed-reader residuals (seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, seed_jit_typed_optional_holding_user_none_takes_some_arm_2026-11-27). Perf on that seed vs base aa542919a298e130, 4e8 matches, min over 10-12 alternated rounds on a loaded host (load 31-37), ms: 30 None-first enums Col.Red subject 1461 / 1476 (+1.0%); no None-owning enum 1463 / 1462; same-code typed control 1459 / 1462. Compiler lib rerun of the 24 earlier failures with --test-threads=1: 11 remain (collection_capture, module_loader nogc_sync_mut io, 2 mir::reachability, object_cache_slice reuse, bootstrap mutex capsule ABI set, 4 core-lane probes, runtime bundle hosted); none of those files reference the changed symbols, the core-lane ones reproduce with the pre-change runtime sources; NOT diffed by name against a base run. Not run: native end-to-end (admission refuses an entry outside the checkout), C lane beyond clang -fsyntax-only, LLVM backend beyond cargo check --features llvm. Deploy: programs building a user None variant reference rt_enum_new_none, so seed and runtime archive must be deployed together."
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 opus-erasedf64 fix (work/bug-erased-f64-none-20261127): new Lowerer::erased_none_arm_condition (hir/lower/expr/control.rs) for a bare None / Option.None / nil arm over an ANY subject, statement and expression forms: rt_is_none(s) first; else rt_enum_id(s) < 2 -> no match; else OR of rt_enum_check_variant(s, E, E's None disc) per user enum E declaring None (user_option_shaped_enums now also records the None discriminant). Explicitly named arms (Opt.None) and typed subjects are unchanged; no shaped enum -> plain rt_is_none. Red->green: seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs jit_bare_none_arm_matches_user_enum_none_through_untyped_parameter SIGABRT -> 4556312, jit_nil_arm_matches_user_enum_none_through_untyped_parameter -846 -> 5153; native_project tests.rs erased_none_arm_user_enum_identity_survives_runtime_name_qualification SIGABRT -> 4563. Seed f391cc81a8b1f257: probes n1 4 -5 -5, n2 4 -5, n3 -5 1 equal the interpreter. Lib 5199 run: failures are the base set (base 23, fix 18; one extra, process_run_bounded_timeout_kills_descendant_process_group, passes alone; repeated_import_of_the_same_module_parses_it_exactly_once flaked once in a filtered run, passes alone 3/3). Perf 3 alternated rounds vs base aa542919a298e130, 4e7 erased matches: no Some/None-owning enum 0.17/0.17/0.24 base vs 0.17/0.21/0.18s fix; None-only enum declared, raw subjects 0.23/0.23/0.24 vs 0.22/0.24/0.22s; Q.None subjects (base aborts) 0.54/0.52/0.53s; RSS flat (41 MB)."

